@startuml
title Refresh Token - /api/v1/auth/refresh POST (AllowAnonymous)

start

:Controller receives Refresh request;

note right
Input Field:
- RefreshToken
end note

:Send RefreshTokenCommand to MediatR;

:Validate command data;

if (Validation failed?) then (Yes)

    :Return 400 Bad Request - Validation failed;
    stop

endif

:RefreshTokenHandler executes;

:Call Auth Service to get RefreshToken by token value;

if (Token exist and is active?) then (Yes)

    :Fetch User associated with the token;

    :Fetch user role;

    :Call JWT Helper to generate new Access and Refresh token;

    :Call Auth Service to revoke the old RefreshToken;

    :Create new RefreshToken entity;

    note right
    RefreshToken Entity Mapping:
    - UserId -> UserId
    - response.RefreshToken -> Token
    - DateTime.UtcNow + ExpiryDays -> ExpiryDate
    - false -> IsRevoked
    end note

    :Call Auth Service to add new RefreshToken;

    :Call Auth Service to SaveChanges;

    :Return 200 OK - New authentication token;

else (No)

    :Return 401 Unauthorized - Invalid or expired refresh token;
    stop

endif

stop

@enduml
